WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

NOTE Descriptive captions for a silent animation. Timings match wilkes_basin_3d_animation_intro_web.mp4 (44.4 s). Vertical exaggeration 100x.

00:00.000 --> 00:03.100
Antarctica from high above the South Pole.
Ice surface coloured by elevation.

00:03.100 --> 00:07.300
The camera swings down towards George V Land,
East Antarctica.

00:07.300 --> 00:09.400
The Wilkes Subglacial Basin region: ice sheet,
ice shelves and ocean. Purple to yellow lines
show ice flow speed (20–500 m per year).

00:09.400 --> 00:15.000
Flying to Mertz Glacier. Ice streams
converge into the outlet glacier.

00:15.000 --> 00:19.900
Ninnis Glacier and its ice shelf.
Fast ice flow drains the interior.

00:19.900 --> 00:24.800
Cook Glacier and Cook Ice Shelf,
at the mouth of the basin.

00:24.800 --> 00:29.700
Pulling back to the regional view.

00:29.700 --> 00:34.000
The ice sheet lifts off its bed.
Bedrock appears beneath: blue below
sea level, green and brown above.

00:34.000 --> 00:36.700
The bed of the Wilkes Subglacial Basin,
held by exposed rock at its edges.

00:36.700 --> 00:41.000
Zooming to the basin floor, with the
Transantarctic Mountains rising on the left.

00:41.000 --> 00:44.400
Wilkes Subglacial Basin: a deep marine basin
under the East Antarctic Ice Sheet.
